OL,4,CWe won't stop - family of abuse        
OL,5,Csurvivor with brain injury call for    
OL,6,Ctougher sentences                      
OL,7,GThe family of a woman left with a      
OL,8,Gserious brain injury after a suspected 
OL,9,Gsuicide attempt following a catalogue  
OL,10,Gof abuse from her former partner is    
OL,11,Gcalling for his sentence to be         
OL,12,Greviewed and stronger penalties for    
OL,13,Gperpetrators.                          
OL,15,FNatasha Farah, 31, has been            
OL,16,Funresponsive in hospital since being   
OL,17,Ffound unconscious at her flat in Rhos- 
OL,18,Fon-Sea, Conwy, in April.               
OL,22,                                   G2/4 
