OL,4,CGovernment blocks export of landmark   
OL,5,CWelsh painting in bid to save it       
OL,6,GA painting believed to be the earliest 
OL,7,Gknown British country estate landscape 
OL,8,Ghas been barred from export to give a  
OL,9,Ggallery or institution the chance to   
OL,10,Gacquire it, the UK government has said.
OL,12,FThe bird's-eye view landscape artwork  
OL,13,Fof Llannerch Park, in Denbighshire,    
OL,14,Fnorth Wales, was completed in 1662 and 
OL,15,Fdepicts the house and Italian-style    
OL,16,Fgardens.                               
OL,18,FIt has been described as an            
OL,19,F"extraordinary window into the         
OL,20,Fdevelopment of gardens" and a heritage 
OL,21,Fexpert said it was "the only surviving 
OL,22,Fevidence of a radical Welsh gardenG4/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
